course: dictionary
lesson: 9976
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives two meanings for teapot: a pot for making tea, and a children's song. Context, the words around it, tells you which one the writer means.
explain: «She walks off; looking back, she sees them trying to stuff the Dormouse into the teapot.» You can stuff something into a teapot only if it is an object, so here teapot means the pot for tea.
explain: «Scorpius, with red Antares, and Sagittarius, shaped like a teapot, lie low in the south in summer» uses teapot to describe a shape. Here the writer means that Sagittarius looks like a teapot.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Put your meaning into the sentence in place of the word and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A teapot is a pot with a handle, a lid and a spout.
fact: You use a teapot to make tea and pour it out.
fact: «I'm a Little Teapot» is a children's song with actions.
fact: A hot teapot can scald you, so be careful when you pour.
fact: In the US, «a storm in a teapot» means a big fuss about nothing; in the UK people say «a storm in a teacup».
exercise: «She walks off; looking back, she sees them trying to stuff the Dormouse into the teapot.» What is the teapot in this sentence? | A small cup | A children's song | A kind of star | *A pot with a handle, a lid and a spout, for making tea
exercise: Ruby says, «I'm a Little Teapot» is a teapot. What is «I'm a Little Teapot»? | A type of tea | A loud shout | A story about a dormouse | *A children's song with actions
exercise: «Sagittarius, shaped like a teapot, lies low in the south in summer.» What does shaped like a teapot mean? | Lives inside a teapot | *Looks like a teapot | Holds a lot of water | Made of tea
test: Which part is part of a teapot? | A keyboard | *A spout | Wheels | A tail
test: In the US, what does «a storm in a teapot» mean? | *A big fuss about nothing | A real storm with heavy rain | A pot of tea left out too long | A loud song
exam: «The teapot was hot, so she used a cloth to lift it.» Which meaning fits? | *A pot for making tea | A children's song | A storm | A type of mug
